## 5. Clarity the new form created

### 5.1 Documentation timeliness is measurable for the first time

The old form's date field mirrors record creation time (in 2024/25 every computable treatment-to-creation delta is approximately zero, and only 460 of 1,688 rows carry the field). The new form records treatment time independently.

| Measure (completed cases, n=1,420) | Result |
|---|---|
| Documented within 1 hour of treatment | 1,235 (87.0%) |
| 1 to 3 hours | 93 |
| 3 to 8 hours | 38 |
| 8 to 24 hours | 13 |
| 24 hours or more | 38 (section 7) |
| Treatment time later than form creation (entry errors, excluded) | 3 |
| Major incidents within 1 hour | 76.7% |
| Minor incidents within 1 hour | 89.0% |

### 5.2 Completion state is visible

Old-form exports show every record as completed because the old workflow had no visible open state. The new workflow exposes it: 1,420 of 1,494 lodged forms (95.0 per cent) completed and 74 open (section 8). Median time from creation to last edit is 4 minutes (quartiles 3 and 12 minutes); 85.2 per cent of completed forms were finalised within an hour of being opened.

### 5.3 Structured data replaced a free-text catch-all

96.4 per cent of 2024/25 cases carried a free-text narrative. Under the new form only 15.8 per cent of completed cases need one; the same information lands in queryable fields, which is what makes section 4 possible.

### 5.4 Medication, oxygen, outcomes and welfare

- Methoxyflurane: 14 records with vial numbers, dose times, administering member, contraindications and adverse effects. Eight carry a starting pain score (mean 7.1 of 10, falling 2.6 points by four minutes across the seven with a four-minute score); six have no score entered. The old form recorded roughly 20 Penthrane administrations in 2024/25 as a bare treatment tag.
- Oxygen: 47 administration records (therapy mask 37, bag valve mask 5, oxygen tubing 3).
- Condition at discharge answered on 98.0 per cent of completed cases (1,379 conscious, 4 deceased, 2 unconscious, 7 other). Condition after treatment recorded on 253 cases; both deteriorations include the mechanism.
- Hospital pathway (211 cases): ambulance handover documented on 117, destination hospital on 65, ambulance case number on 18.
- Responder welfare, asked for the first time: 7 peer-support requests and 1 occupational-violence report.

